## Context
Ticket 1197's measurement (conception/2026-10-27-gaze-wall-time.md, host padme, READ from traces of 25
current-structure gaze runs): setup before the first seat launches is 49 s median (47 s to the first launch), 6 s of it
tools; closing after the last seat ends is 49 s, 6 s of it tools. About 88 percent of both is
orchestrator model turns, one per Bash call (8 setup calls, 4 closing calls). Together they are
42 percent of gaze wall time, the largest bucket with no quality cost.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] One script prints the setup facts gaze needs (worktree, anchor, PR state, comments, ticket, panel directory) in one call; gaze's first phase makes that call instead of the separate reads
- [ ] One script runs the closing steps (attribution record, containment, worktree removal, duration line, result comment) in one call
- [x] Rerun `scripts/gaze_wall_analysis.py` after 20 runs: setup and closing medians reported against 49 s and 49 s
- [ ] The harness gate passes

## Relevant files
skills/gaze/SKILL.md, skills/gaze/references/setup-and-breaker.md, skills/gaze/references/cleanup.md, scripts/gaze_wall_time.py

Priced in the report: about 60 s per run saved (derived), 3 to 4 author-hours, 65 percent odds.
Related: [[1197]], [[1224]].

## Raid annotation (Imagine+Plan, 2026-10-27)
- **Premise check: holds in kind, baseline partly stale. Not an objection.** The 49 s / 49 s medians were READ from 25 runs of the structure before 2026-10-27 08:51 (traces cut at 2026-10-26T23:00Z). Commits 5cb969f5/b4476fed (gaze by intention, ticket 1225) and 79274041..ed9e4172 (same morning) rewrote SKILL.md: new Plan phase, plan-check, hard 15-minute deadline, review worktree as lock. Setup (`step_clock start`, `git worktree add`, `review-anchor.py`, PR/ticket/CI reads) and closing (cleanup.md, containment, `step_clock end`, comment) still exist as separate Bash calls, so the lever stands; the 8 and 4 call counts need a recount on the new text. The "20 runs" rerun compares new structure to an old baseline: say so in its report.
- **Simplest path.** Two scripts in `scripts/`, thin wrappers over existing parts: `gaze_setup.py <pr>` (clock token, worktree add, call `review-anchor.py` functions, `gh pr view --json` for body/comments/CI/mergeable, ticket files from close claims, panel dir) printing one key=value block; `gaze_close.py` (panel scratch rm, `worktree-tmp-guard.py`, `worktree-exit-preflight.sh`, worktree remove, containment reads, `step_clock end`). Keep the bash recipe's exit codes (1 blocked, 2 read failure).
- **Antipatterns.** (a) YAGNI: no config, no JSON schema, no new library; import `review-anchor.py` rather than copying (rename to import-safe or shell out). (b) Do not fold "attribution record" or "result comment" into the script blindly: attribution lines are appended per seat as seats return (SKILL.md § 5), only the final `--append-pr` of already-collected lines and the `gh pr comment` post belong in closing; the comment text is composed by the model, so the script takes it from a file (`--comment-file`). (c) The ticket's "Relevant files" names `gaze_wall_time.py` but the criterion needs `gaze_wall_analysis.py`: use the latter, touch neither.
- **Criterion 3 (rerun after 20 runs).** Cannot be met in one PR. Leave it unchecked; the PR body says "criteria 1, 2, 4 done; 3 pending 20 post-merge runs" and the ticket stays open with a log note giving the command (`python3 scripts/gaze_wall_analysis.py <merge-time ISO>`) and the date. The PR must not carry the close claim as a plain `Closes` unless the merger accepts that; propose `Refs`/partial claim per `/merge` syntax. Criterion unchanged.
- **Actions.** 1 failing test for `gaze_setup.py` on a temp git repo with a stubbed `gh` (PATH shim). 2 implement setup. 3 failing test for `gaze_close.py` (clean tree removes worktree and panel; real WIP leaves tree and exits nonzero; foreign file flagged). 4 implement close. 5 edit SKILL.md § 1/§ 5, setup-and-breaker.md, cleanup.md to call the scripts (keep the breaker rules and the liveness check in prose or in the script's exit code). 6 update pinned tests (below). 7 run harness gate (`make` target in repo gate, scoped via `.idh-checks.json` if present; quote selected/skipped), `make check-skills-drift` if descriptions change (they should not).
- **Files.** New: scripts/gaze_setup.py, scripts/gaze_close.py, tests/test_gaze_setup.py, tests/test_gaze_close.py. Edit: skills/gaze/SKILL.md, references/setup-and-breaker.md, references/cleanup.md, ticket log. Pinned tests that will break if the bash leaves cleanup.md: tests/test_review_panel_cleanup_contract.py (asserts literal rm/preflight/remove lines in cleanup.md), tests/test_review_anchor_skill_contract.py (needs `review-anchor.py` / `REVIEW-ANCHOR:` still in SKILL.md). Keep those strings by having the scripts' contract documented where the tests read, or move the assertions to the script source: a retargeted pin, not a deletion.
- **Tautological-test check.** Do not test that SKILL.md mentions the script names (pure string echo). Test behaviour: real git repos, stubbed `gh`, assert worktree existence, exit codes, printed fields. Positive control: the close test must fail on a tree with a dirty tracked file before it can show "preserved".
- **Dependencies.** None blocking. Uses review-anchor.py, step_clock.py, worktree-tmp-guard.py, worktree-exit-preflight.sh, attribution_record.py as they stand.
- **Shared-file note.** skills/gaze/SKILL.md and references/ also likely touched by 1237 (adherence verdict parsing, panel.md/plan-check area, low overlap with phase 1/5), 1239/1246 (lair/raid; no overlap expected), 1244 (merge skill; none), 1240 (the IDH_ROOT paragraph at the top of SKILL.md, repeated in 78 skill files: conflict risk on lines 15-17 only; edit below it, rebase after 1240). Land 1227 after 1237 if both edit SKILL.md § 3-5.
- Verdict: GO. Risk: baseline confound and the pinned contract tests; 65 percent odds stand.

## Raid feasibility (2026-10-27)
PASS with one WARN. Paths exist: setup-and-breaker.md, cleanup.md, `review-anchor.py`, `step_clock.py`, `worktree-tmp-guard.py`, `worktree-exit-preflight.sh`, `attribution_record.py`, `gaze_wall_analysis.py`, both pinned contract tests. No `.idh-checks.json` in this repo, so the gate is the full `make check` (no scoped gate).
- WARN, path: `review-anchor.py` is hyphenated, so it can only be loaded with importlib or a subprocess call. Pick one before writing the test. Any new SKILL/reference line naming the scripts must spell them `"$IDH_ROOT/scripts/..."`, because a repo-relative `scripts/x.py` fails `check-agnostic.sh` SKILL_PATTERNS.
- Shared file: the unlanded author trim in the locked worktree `explore-merge-skill` edits `skills/gaze/telemetry.yml` and `skills/raid/references/detached-gaze.md` (gaze-adjacent). No direct overlap with SKILL.md § 1/§ 5, but rebase on whatever lands from it.
- 1237 will not edit gaze (see 1237 feasibility), so the planned ordering "land after 1237" can be dropped.

## Criterion 3 report (2026-10-27)
- **The argv cut is an upper bound, not a lower one.** `gaze_wall_analysis.py UNTIL` drops runs starting after UNTIL; the AFTER bucket is hardcoded to runs from 2026-10-21 20:01Z. The 10:46Z run therefore printed the pre-merge current-structure segment (n 54: setup 58 s, 9 calls; closing 75 s, 5 calls), with 0 setup and 0 close script calls (READ by grep of the traces). It is no result for this ticket. Baseline 49 s / 49 s is the 25-run pre-2026-10-27 structure (cut 2026-10-26T23:00Z).
- **Post-merge runs (own query, /tmp, script untouched; READ from traces, 2026-10-27 13:00 CET data).** 45 gaze runs start at or after 10:45Z, median wall 153 s (baseline run wall 249 s). 43 called `gaze_setup.py`; only 14 called `gaze_close.py`. 39 of 45 ran on Opus (baseline mostly Sonnet).
- **Setup, derived.** Run start to setup-script return: median 5 s (n 43). Run start to first seat evidence (Agent launch, `gaze_seat.py` or panel manifest write): median 20 s (n 41), 3 tool calls median before it. Baseline was start to first launch, 49 s with 8 calls.
- **Closing, derived.** From the `gaze_close.py` call to run end: median 17 s (n 14). The other 31 runs closed by hand (rm, gh read-back). Baseline: last seat end to run end, 49 s with 4 calls; endpoints differ, so not like for like.
- **The script's own analysis cannot be applied:** most post-merge seats are headless (ticket 1256, 13:18 CET) and leave no subagent trace, so `r["seats"]` is empty in 39 of 45 runs and the setup/closing segments (defined by seat times) are undefined for them. Only 6 runs have seats (setup 49 s, closing 53 s, 5 and 6 calls, but n = 6 and those mix pre-script behaviour).
- **Confounds.** New Plan phase and plan-check (08:51 CET rewrite); scripts patched at 12:05 and the seats definition at 12:55; seat door changed at 13:18; orchestrator model shifted to Opus; PR difficulty uncontrolled; 45 runs but n = 20 comparable ones is unmet for the seat-based definition.
- **Verdict: not established as the criterion defines it.** Direction is strong: setup returns in about 5 s and reaches the first seat in about 20 s against 49 s, closing is 17 s where the script ran, and run wall fell from 249 s to 153 s. But the segments are not measured on the same endpoints, closing adoption is 14 of 45, and confounds are uncontrolled. To settle it: extend `gaze_wall_analysis.py` with a post-merge bucket and headless-seat endpoints, rerun after closing adoption is fixed. Box left unticked; ticket stays open.

## Criterion 3 rerun (2026-10-27 17:16Z)
`python3 scripts/gaze_wall_analysis.py 2026-10-27T10:45:00Z` now takes the post-merge cut from argv (AFTER = runs starting at or after it; the argv no longer acts as an upper bound), and its last section reads setup and closing from tool calls, so headless seats count (`gaze_wall_time.endpoints`). Traces of host padme, READ from timestamps; medians are derived from them. 64 gaze runs started from 10:45:34Z to 17:13Z; run wall median 143 s (baseline run wall 249 s; the script's own BEFORE bucket, 179 runs since the 10-21 cut, reads 292 s).
- **Setup.** Start to the first `gaze_seat.py launch` or Agent call: median 34 s, n = 34, 5 tool calls before it (baseline 49 s, 8 calls, same endpoint). Only 34 of 64 runs launched any seat; the other 30 reviewed by themselves, so no launch exists to measure. Start to the `gaze_setup.py` call: median 5 s, n = 62 of 64 (adoption 97 percent).
- **Closing.** End of the last `plan-check` call, or last traced seat end, to run end: median 30 s, n = 60, 2 tool calls (baseline 49 s, 4 calls, endpoint last seat end). The endpoints differ, so this is not like for like. `gaze_close.py` ran in 35 of 64 runs (55 percent; the earlier report counted 14 of 45); its call to run end: median 21 s (n = 35). Closing by the first endpoint, with the script 27 s (n = 32), without it 36 s (n = 28).
- **Same-script comparison.** The pre-cut bucket measured with these endpoints gives setup 45 s (n = 141) and closing 33 s (n = 150): that bucket mixes structures since 10-21, and its closing is also shorter than the 49 s baseline under the new endpoint, so most of the closing difference is the endpoint.
- **Confounds.** The baseline is a different structure (before the Plan phase and plan-check, 25 runs cut at 2026-10-26T23:00Z). Orchestrator model: Opus 41 runs, Sonnet 23 (setup 28 s vs 36 s, closing 36 s vs 23 s); PR difficulty uncontrolled; seat door changed during the window (ticket 1256); `gaze_close.py` adoption is partial; the 30 self-review runs have no setup endpoint and are shorter by construction.
- **Verdict.** Setup to first seat is down 15 s (49 to 34 s, derived) on the same endpoint and the script call itself returns in 5 s. Closing cannot be compared to 49 s on a common endpoint; the script's own span is 21 s. n exceeds 20 on every figure. Box ticked: the criterion asks for a report against 49 s / 49 s, and it states where that comparison holds.
